# Instructions-only chat — no RE, PR, LF, login

Some workspace chats are **rules/configuration only** (agent directives, skill updates, transfer-matrix changes, Case Tracker setup, etc.). **This is not the customer-case processing chat.**

## When this rule applies

Treat the current chat as **instructions-only** when **any** of these is true:

1. The user **previously stated** this chat is for rules/configuration only (e.g. "this chat is for rule configuration ONLY", "do not process RE/PR/LF here").
2. The conversation is **clearly** about rules, skills, config, or automation design — **not** an active Sprinklr case thread (no visible-case RE workflow in progress for paste/send).
3. The user is asking to **retain/update rules** or agent behaviour (like this directive).

When in doubt in a mixed thread: if the user sends **only** `RE`, `PR`, `LF`, or `login` without rules context → **warn and refuse** case processing.

## Blocked commands (do not run scripts or automation)

| Command | Blocked action |
|---------|----------------|
| **RE** / **re** | read-email script, 7-step case output |
| **PR** / **pr** | paste reply, write-reply script |
| **LF** / **lf** | fill_case_tracker.py, log form |
| **login** | Sprinklr login-only / startup automation |

Also do **not** partially run case steps (no CDP Sprinklr reads "just to check" unless explicitly for **rules/testing documentation** the user asked for in this chat).

## Mandatory warning (use every time)

When the user triggers a blocked command in an instructions-only chat, **do not process it**. Reply with this (or equivalent) **before anything else**:

```
⚠️ Wrong chat — this thread is for rules and configuration only, not Sprinklr login or email processing (RE / PR / LF).

Open a separate chat for customer cases, then run your command there.
```

If the user also asked a rules/config question in the same message, answer that **after** the warning.

## What IS allowed here

- Updating `.cursor/rules/`, skills, AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS, TransferMatrix, config structure (not live case handling)
- Explaining how RE/PR/LF/login work
- Documenting test results from configuration work **without** treating the chat as the live processing queue

## Customer-case chats

Other chats where the user is actively processing a visible Sprinklr case (RE → PR → LF flow) follow the normal RE/PR/LF rules. This file does not disable those chats — only prevents **mistaken** use of an instructions-only thread.
